From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FramePlayer contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] xr: don't discard the shared buffer's depth/stencil on
 Linux

XRWebGLDrawingBuffer::DoneWithSharedBuffer() discards the depth and stencil
attachments of the WebXR framebuffer before handing the shared buffer to
the XR service. On Linux the shared buffer is a Vulkan image that the
OpenXR service copies into the runtime's swapchain from its own device.
With ANGLE on desktop GL over zink (Steam Frame: Turnip, Adreno 750) the
discard also lost colour rendering that was still in flight: in an
XRWebGLLayer session the right eye (drawn last) came through black or
flickering, and late passes such as water were missing. Simple scenes were
unaffected, which hid it.

Verified on a Steam Frame with headset captures of an IWSDK/three.js r184
game: right eye black in 7 of 8 captures with the discard (also with a
glFinish() after it), both eyes complete in 8 of 8 without it. Calling
gl.finish() from the page before Blink's end-of-frame work also fixed it,
pointing at the discard rather than a missing GPU fence.

Skip the discard on Linux; it is only a bandwidth hint.

Bug: none
---
 .../renderer/platform/graphics/gpu/xr_webgl_drawing_buffer.cc    | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/gpu/xr_webgl_drawing_buffer.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/gpu/xr_webgl_drawing_buffer.cc
index 1470d471c7..ef75b15426 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/gpu/xr_webgl_drawing_buffer.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/gpu/xr_webgl_drawing_buffer.cc
@@ -331,7 +331,14 @@ XRWebGLDrawingBuffer::DoneWithSharedBuffer() {
   // Discard the depth and stencil attachments since we're done with them.
   // Don't discard the color buffer, we do need this rendered into the
   // shared buffer.
-  if (discard_framebuffer_supported_) {
+  //
+  // Not on Linux: there the shared buffer is a Vulkan image the OpenXR service
+  // copies from another device, and with ANGLE on desktop GL over zink (Steam
+  // Frame: Turnip, Adreno 750) the discard also loses colour rendering that is
+  // still in flight. The eye drawn last came through black or flickering and
+  // late passes such as water were missing. Skipping a discard only costs
+  // bandwidth.
+  if (discard_framebuffer_supported_ && !BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)) {
     const GLenum kAttachments[3] = {GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT, GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT};
     gl->BindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, framebuffer_);
     gl->DiscardFramebufferEXT(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 2, kAttachments);
